<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Taeil wins $1.2 bln order from Silmag.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Taeil wins $1.2 bln order from Silmag.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Taeil Media Co Ltd said on Thursday it had won a $1.2 billion order from France's high-tech company Silmag to provide magnetic heads for hard disk drives until the year 2000.  </p>
<p>Taeil Media said in a statement the shipments were scheduled to begin in December.</p>
<p>Under the contract, Taeil is due to deliver 200 million magnetic heads by 2000, it said.</p>
<p>Taeil is a manufacturer of various computer parts such as hard disk drive heads and hard disks.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
